ort"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_16", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "1885 emits a single event (to 749) at ~23384-23483. Reaching 1460 needs >=4-5 hops through bridges 1453/1871/1085, but 1453's entire activity precedes 22883 and 1871's ends by 24083, so no forward-ordered chain leaves 1885's side after it acted. Decisively, 1460's only feasible in-event (632->1460) occurs at >=24684 while every incoming event at 632 is <=23483, a gap of >1200 units, far exceeding the 600-unit maximum latency. A time-ignoring path and heavy local volume exist, but no time-respecting cascade does."}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**Structure.** Node 1885 has exactly one event in the window: 1885\u2192749 (step_02, step_03). Node 1460 has three events, with partners {252, 632, 765} (step_02, step_04). The 3-hop neighbourhoods of 1885 (step_05) and 1460 (step_08) are nearly disjoint \u2014 they only meet at bridge nodes 1085, 1453, 1871 \u2014 so any 1885\u21921460 route is \u22654\u20135 hops.\n\n**Timing of the source.** 1885's single event is localized to [23384, 23483] (steps 06, 09, 11). Anything carrying its influence must occur *after* ~23384.\n\n**Bridge 1453 / 1871 is temporally dead.** All of 1453's activity falls in [18083, 22883] (step_12), i.e. entirely *before* 1885 acted, so 749\u21921453\u21921871 cannot transmit influence forward. 1871's events all end by 24083 (step_13).\n\n**The final hop breaks the \u2264600 delay rule.** 1460's only in-event from 632 lies in [24084, 25283] (step_10) and, intersected with 632's activity profile, in [24684, 25283] (step_14, step_16). But every *incoming* event to 632 occurs at or before 23483 (step_14: zero 632 activity in [23484, 24683]). The gap from any possible predecessor event at 632 to 632\u21921460 is therefore \u22651200 time units \u2014 twice the permitted 600-unit latency. The alternative in-edge (765\u21921460) sits in a sub-cluster reachable only through 1871/488/1735/384, whose activity likewise ends by 24083.\n\n**Confounder controls.** The window is busy (2186 events, 1500 active nodes, step_01) and 1885's neighbour 749 sits next to the mega-hub 1566 (step_05), and there is a static ignoring-time path 1885\u2192749\u21921453\u21921871\u2192632\u21921460. Local burstiness around 23384\u201325183 is also present (step_15: 17, 5, 6 events). None of this yields an ordered, \u2264600-gap chain: the volume and the static connectivity are real, but the required timestamps are ordered wrongly or too far apart.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_e2469334\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1885, 1460, 749, 632, 1453, 1871, 765],\n  \"window\": [18083, 27683],\n  \"confidence\": 0.76,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"1885 emits a single event (to 749) at ~23384-23483. Reaching 1460 needs >=4-5 hops through bridges 1453/1871/1085, but 1453's entire activity precedes 22883 and 1871's ends by 24083, so no forward-ordered chain leaves 1885's side after it acted. Decisively, 1460's only feasible in-event (632->1460) occurs at >=24684 while every incoming event at 632 is <=23483, a gap of >1200 units, far exceeding the 600-unit maximum latency. A time-ignoring path and heavy local volume exist, but no time-respecting cascade does.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 38103, "total_output_tokens": 9274, "total_tokens": 47377, "total_latency_ms": 124107, "llm_calls": 7, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}